WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.560
Following Betty White's death on December 31,&nbsp;
2021, Bob Saget penned a heartfelt tribute to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.160
the comedy icon. Ten days later, the comedy&nbsp;
world is mourning the loss of Saget himself.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.720
For decades, Saget was known for his edgy&nbsp;
stand-up comedy, his long-running hosting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:22.160
stint on America's Funniest Home Videos, and&nbsp;
memorable roles as Danny Tanner on Full House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.120
and as the narrator on How I Met Your Mother.&nbsp;
Saget was actively working as an entertainer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.720
up until the time of his death.&nbsp;
Before he unexpectedly passed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.920
he was set to continue his nationwide&nbsp;
stand-up tour into the spring of 2022.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.800
Now, the world is in shock at the sudden loss of&nbsp;
the beloved performer. The unexpected death lands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.400
even harder, since it seems like Saget had begun&nbsp;
to hit his stride on his latest comedy tour, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.920
appeared to be gearing up for a new phase of his&nbsp;
career with a renewed focus on live performance.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:55.680
After performing what would ultimately&nbsp;
be his final show, Saget tweeted:

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.000
"Loved tonight’s show&nbsp;
PV_ConcertHall in Jacksonville.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.920
Appreciative audience. Thanks again&nbsp;
to RealTimWilkins for opening.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:09.440
I had no idea I did a 2 hr set tonight.&nbsp;
I’m happily addicted again to this s—."

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.160
Condolences and remembrances have been pouring&nbsp;
in from fans and fellow Hollywood stars in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:20.160
wake of this tragedy, a mere 10 days after Saget&nbsp;
himself mourned the loss of another comedy giant:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.320
Betty White, who died a few&nbsp;
weeks shy of her 100th birthday.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.480
"I'm an old lady to the rest of the&nbsp;
world but to me I'm just a girl."

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.280
In the days following White's death,&nbsp;
Saget shared his memories of White on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.920
his Instagram. In the tribute, the famously&nbsp;
blue comedian recalled a story where he and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:42.480
White were on a private jet drinking Bloody&nbsp;
Marys and laughing together. He wrote,

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.040
"I looked into her eyes and faux romantically&nbsp;
said, 'How 'bout it, Betty, you and me in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.000
bathroom? Mile High Club?' She answered me before&nbsp;
I had a chance to finish the invite — 'Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.760
Bob, you go in there first and I'll&nbsp;
meet you as soon as I finish my drink.'"

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.560
Saget went on to jokingly add that Betty continued&nbsp;
sipping her drink while he waited in the bathroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.520
for what he claimed was over two hours. Assuming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.000
that his joke might be taken totally out&nbsp;
of context, the actor went on to clarify,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.840
"That would be the joke on a joke part,&nbsp;
in case you take things literally."

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.320
Beyond recollecting this humorous encounter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.240
Saget more seriously mused on White's&nbsp;
view of the afterlife. He continued,

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:23.520
"She always said the love of her life was her&nbsp;
husband, Allen Ludden, who she lost in 1981.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.960
Well, if things work out by Betty's&nbsp;
design [...] they are reunited.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.000
I don't know what happens when we&nbsp;
die, but if Betty says you get to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.360
be with the love of your life, then&nbsp;
I happily defer to Betty on this."

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.520
No one could have known the world&nbsp;
would lose Saget just a few days later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.920
and it's especially emotional to read these&nbsp;
words now. Fans have already taken to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:47.040
Instagram post's comments section to express&nbsp;
their grief over the surprising loss of Saget.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.160
Even before Saget's death, fans were showing up&nbsp;
in droves for his Instagram post honoring Betty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:57.040
White. Now that his poignant words have accrued&nbsp;
additional weight in the wake of his passing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.520
that fan response has become even more&nbsp;
overwhelming. Many commenters picked up on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.000
White's hopeful impression of the afterlife&nbsp;
and ran with it, wishing Saget well in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.280
reunion with one of his comedy idols. One&nbsp;
commenter with the handle youngeds wrote:

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.680
"Together now drinking bloody Mary's&nbsp;
in heaven may you both Rest In Peace."

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.560
Another commenter that goes by tufftopic added:

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.640
"Wow! You two are now angels&nbsp;
and will meet again! Rip Bob!."

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.480
Despite coming from different generations,&nbsp;
Saget and White clearly touched many of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.640
same lives and shared many fans as&nbsp;
a result. The comments that didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.400
specifically focus on the heavenly&nbsp;
reunion between the two blue comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:40.400
simply used the space to honor Saget. A user&nbsp;
with the handle jeimbinder wrote in the comments:

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.440
"gonna miss you man. You&nbsp;
brought so many smiles. Rip."

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.880
The comedy world is reeling from the loss&nbsp;
of two titans in such close proximity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.440
but if Betty White was right — and, honestly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:58.000
when wasn't she? — they just might be cracking&nbsp;
each other up on another plane of existence.

